WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.310
You may have heard that
the oceans are acidifying.

2
00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:06.430
Burning fuels releases
extra carbon dioxide,

3
00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:09.990
and the oceans absorb part
of it, year after year.

4
00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:13.890
Yet test seawater today,
and it is still alkaline.

5
00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:18.350
So if the oceans are acidifying,
why is seawater still alkaline?

6
00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:21.510
In this mission, you'll
sort oxides into basic,

7
00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:25.970
acidic and amphoteric, and follow
the change across period 3.

8
00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:28.350
You'll trace acid rain
back to its sources,

9
00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:32.910
and find out what happens when
carbon dioxide dissolves in water.

10
00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:37.150
Your mission: explain what ocean
acidification really means.
